    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2RiZDVd8Fb6BcQM4DoVrfQ5)_\n\nFollows #55 (merged), which this was stacked on; the base is now `main`.\n\n## Summary\n- The 36 provide subsections that sit inside topical sections (after #52 handled the top-level ones) now have the heading `Provide`, a one-line summary and one source block. In `sp-magit-style`, \"Hooks, and provide\" becomes \"Hooks\" plus a separate `Provide`. `sp-relationship-annotator` is left alone: its provide entry belongs to a line-by-line walkthrough.\n- `docs/main.org` gets a \"Writing the Provide section of a module doc\" section with the convention.\n- The review guide (project file) gets the same rule as a checklist.\n\n## Verification\nTangling every doc before and after produces identical `.el` files under `libraries/modules/`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01ACbiw1tHxZUgAEj5duertR",
